      "sourceTextSha256": "bfc1794feef02e988b3bfd1255fa22c3c0c6ab2075bf3391705f43c0a1b49f54",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw8vu04w",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "At the scheduled time, transfer to the bus station for the journey to San Juan.\n\nOn arrival, you’ll be met and taken to your hotel to check in and rest. Then head out on a city tour.\n\nJuan Jufré founded San Juan in the late 16th century and named it after John the Baptist. The main sights include St John’s Cathedral, the Franklin Library, often described as the oldest library in South America, and the Félix Aguilar Observatory.\n\nReturn to the hotel after the tour."
    },
